<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">This Land Is Your Land (the Travellers)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1956</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Canadian version with new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Recordings by Bob Dylan, the Kingston Trio, Trini Lopez, Jay and the Americans and the New Christy Minstrels</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1960s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">covers</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">This Land Is Your Land (Peter, Paul and Mary, on Moving)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1962</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">This Land Is Your Land (the Seekers, on A World of Our Own)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1965</span><span class="sg-chain-h">cover</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bound for Glory (film, Hal Ashby)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1976</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung in the closing credits</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">This Land Is Your Land (Bruce Springsteen, on Live/1975–85)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">live recording</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">This badge is your badge (Mickey O'Farrell)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">football supporters' version for FC United of Manchester</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">JibJab election parody</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2004</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">God Bless America (Irving Berlin)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the song it answered</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">When the World's on Fire (the Carter Family)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">source of the melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Oh, My Loving Brother</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Baptist gospel hymn behind the Carter Family's melody</span></li></ul></section>
